NAME
    passwd - set an account password

SYNOPSIS
    passwd <newpassword>
    passwd <name> <newpassword>

DESCRIPTION
    Stores a password hash for the current session's account (one
    argument) or, when running as root, for <name>'s account (two
    arguments).

    Passwords are passed as a command argument rather than read from a
    masked prompt, so they appear in command history(1). Account
    passwords are stored in memory for the lifetime of the process and
    are not currently prompted for by su(1).

EXAMPLES
    passwd newpass
    passwd guest guestpass

EXIT STATUS
    0   Password updated.
    1   Invalid usage, non-root attempt to change another account's
        password, or target account does not exist.

SEE ALSO
    su(1), useradd(1), userdel(1), whoami(1)
